{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":2,"delta":"{\"i\":\"Writing preflight report\",\"path\":\"in/billingdb/preflight_report.md\",\"content\":\"# Billing migration preflight report\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Source tables: `invoices`, `payments`\\n- Target additions: `invoices.status`, `payment_orphans`, foreign-key-safe `payments`\\n\\n## Preflight SQL\\n```sql\\nSELECT 'invoice_count' AS metric, COUNT(*) AS value FROM invoices;\\nSELECT 'payment_count' AS metric, COUNT(*) AS value FROM payments;\\nSELECT 'orphan_payment_count' AS metric, COUNT(*) AS value\\nFROM payments AS p\\nLEFT JOIN invoices AS i ON i.id = p.invoice_id\\nWHERE i.id IS NULL;\\n\\nSELECT p.id, p.invoice_id, p.amount_cents, p.created_at\\nFROM payments AS p\\nLEFT JOIN invoices AS i ON i.id = p.invoice_id\\nWHERE i.id IS NULL\\nORDER BY p.id;\\n```\\n\\n## Observed result from `schema.sql`\\n- `invoices`: 3 rows\\n- `payments`: 4 rows\\n- orphan payments: 1 row\\n- orphan detail preserved by migration: `p4 | missing-invoice | 700 | 2024-01-07T10:00:00Z`\\n\\n## Migration gate\\n- Do not proceed unless the orphan set is understood and intentionally moved into `payment_orphans`.\\n- Do not proceed unless the migration is run as a single explicit transaction.\\n- Do not proceed unless postcheck and rollback scripts are available beside the migration.\\n\"}"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_14YCJ66jrXSPPVGCh6DHHC7Z|fc_0ef86f0825944dfa016a95aec52fe087d2a398067e99c5d4f9","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Writing preflight report","path":"in/billingdb/preflight_report.md","content":"# Billing migration preflight report\n\n## Scope\n- Source tables: `invoices`, `payments`\n- Target additions: `invoices.status`, `payment_orphans`, foreign-key-safe `payments`\n\n## Preflight SQL\n```sql\nSELECT 'invoice_count' AS metric, COUNT(*) AS value FROM invoices;\nSELECT 'payment_count' AS metric, COUNT(*) AS value FROM payments;\nSELECT 'orphan_payment_count' AS metric, COUNT(*) AS value\nFROM payments AS p\nLEFT JOIN invoices AS i ON i.id = p.invoice_id\nWHERE i.id IS NULL;\n\nSELECT p.id, p.invoice_id, p.amount_cents, p.created_at\nFROM payments AS p\nLEFT JOIN invoices AS i ON i.id = p.invoice_id\nWHERE i.id IS NULL\nORDER BY p.id;\n```\n\n## Observed result from `schema.sql`\n- `invoices`: 3 rows\n- `payments`: 4 rows\n- orphan payments: 1 row\n- orphan detail preserved by migration: `p4 | missing-invoice | 700 | 2024-01-07T10:00:00Z`\n\n## Migration gate\n- Do not proceed unless the orphan set is understood and intentionally moved into `payment_orphans`.\n- Do not proceed unless the migration is run as a single explicit transaction.\n- Do not proceed unless postcheck and rollback scripts are available beside the migration.\n"}}}}
